 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that a matrix of rank $5$ must have at least $5$ columns and at least $5$ rows. \nSo, we disregard the matrix $A$ since it has only $3$ rows and the matrix $C$ since it has only $4$ columns. \n\nAlso, the matrix must have $5$ pivot columns. As we can see, the matrix $B$ has exactly $5$ pivot columns. So, $\\text{rank}(B)=5.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$B$ only\"."}]}
